        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8Ve4RREZAQvm6GCoqSIB-77" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fontColor=#000000;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;gradientColor=#FFF2A1;shadow=1;size=20;pointerEvents=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;Questions to ask the professor later&lt;/b&gt;:&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Q1: Do we need to create/keep track of an ID for each instance of &quot;BooksOnCart&quot;?&amp;nbsp; (aka creating ID for the list of books that are in my cart and purchase has not been made yet?) (Do we need to store this information? If yes, how the ID of this class different than the orderID in the OrderSummary?) Can we have the ID for BooksOnCart calculated instantly when people put on the cart?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Q2: Because we do not yet know whether the buyers are already established customers until they check out, our website technically doesn&#39;t remember the cart of guests if they exit the website without making a&amp;nbsp;purchase, right?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Q3: Can a person decide to buy and finish creating an account, but then change their mind and cancelling the check out process? In that case, are their information still being stored in database?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;-Q4: For the relationship &quot;from 1 to 0...1&quot;, when the id previous class transferred to the id of the latter class (similar to the Account class vs. Seller/Buyer class)? When each class will have their own ID?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="380" width="320" x="880" y="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
